course: dictionary
lesson: 6169
title: Less is more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Minimalism is a word for a style that uses very few, simple things and leaves out everything that is not needed. Minimal means as little as possible. Read the context: «Minimalism is art that uses very little, like simple shapes.» The words very little and simple shapes are clues, so minimalism must mean keeping things simple and sparse.
explain: Minimalism can also be a way of living. People who choose it own fewer things and buy only what they really need. Some families do this to save money, to have less clutter, or to care for the environment.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a love of minimalism» still make sense if you think of it as a love of very simple, uncluttered things? Yes, so your meaning fits. Look at phrases like «minimalism in design» to see where the word is used.
fact: Minimalism means using very few, simple shapes, colours or notes, and leaving out what is not needed.
fact: In art, a minimalist work may be just a few lines or blocks of one colour.
fact: In music, minimalism repeats simple patterns that change slowly. Composers Steve Reich and Philip Glass are well known for this style.
fact: As a way of living, minimalism means having fewer things and buying only what you really need.
fact: People can disagree about minimalist art: some think a nearly empty work is deep, and others do not.
exercise: «Minimalism is art that uses very little, like simple shapes.» What does minimalism mean in art? | A way of making things very large | A style full of bright, busy patterns | Art made only from photographs | *A style that uses very few, simple shapes, colours or notes
exercise: Mia's family sold half their toys and now buys only what they need. What lifestyle is this? | Decoration | *Minimalism | Clutter | Luxury
exercise: Which room shows minimalism in design? | *A room with clean, simple lines and only a few things in it | A room full of patterned rugs, plants and posters | A room with the walls covered in mirrors | A room with gold chairs and many lamps
test: In music, minimalism repeats what kind of pattern? | Long, loud crashes | *Simple patterns that change slowly | Lyrics about the weather | Random silence
test: Why might a family choose minimalism? | To have more clutter in the house | To spend more money on new things | *To save money and have less clutter | To fill every corner of the house
exam: Which sentence best explains minimalism? | *Minimalism uses very few, simple things and leaves out what is not needed | Minimalism means painting with many colours | Minimalism is a loud, busy style of music | Minimalism means having as many things as possible
